\nplt.scatter(\n    credit_df[\"credit_utilization\"],\n    credit_df[\"repayment_score\"],\n    c=credit_df[\"default\"],\n    alpha=0.55\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"Credit utilization\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Repayment-history score\")\nplt.title(\"Classification target: Default vs No Default\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.122993Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.123628Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.518625Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.123597Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.517307Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":9},{"id":"07c441c8","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Train a classification model\n\nWe use **Logistic Regression** as a simple baseline.\n\nThe goal today is **not** to study logistic regression in depth.  \nThe goal is to understand what a classification model outputs and how we evaluate it.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"85cb7894","cell_type":"code","source":"classification_features = [\n    \"annual_income\",\n    \"credit_utilization\",\n    \"outstanding_debt\",\n    \"repayment_score\",\n    \"account_age_months\"\n]\n\nX_cls = credit_df[classification_features]\ny_cls = credit_df[\"default\"]\n\nX_train_cls, X_test_cls, y_train_cls, y_test_cls = train_test_split(\n    X_cls,\n    y_cls,\n    test_size=0.20,\n    random_state=42,\n    stratify=y_cls\n)\n\nclassification_model = make_pipeline(\n    StandardScaler(),\n    LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000)\n)\n\nclassification_model.fit(X_train_cls, y_train_cls)\n\ncls_predictions = classification_model.predict(X_test_cls)\ncls_probabilities = classification_model.predict_proba(X_test_cls)[:, 1]\n\nprint(\"Accuracy:\", round(accuracy_score(y_test_cls, cls_predictions), 3))\nprint(\"\\nClassification report:\")\nprint(classification_report(y_test_cls, cls_predictions))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.520029Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.520427Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.567007Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.520378Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.565052Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Accuracy: 0.947\n\nClassification report:\n              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n\n           0       0.97      0.97      0.97       273\n           1       0.70      0.70      0.70        27\n\n    accuracy                           0.95       300\n   macro avg       0.84      0.84      0.84       300\nweighted avg       0.95      0.95      0.95       300\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":10},{"id":"374fb8a4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual 2 — Confusion matrix\n\nA classification model does more than produce an accuracy score.\n\nThe confusion matrix shows:\n\n- correctly predicted non-defaults\n- correctly predicted defaults\n- false alarms\n- missed defaults\n\nThis is especially important in risk-sensitive systems because different mistakes can have very different consequences.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"8b168c68","cell_type":"code","source":"ConfusionMatrixDisplay.from_predictions(\n    y_test_cls,\n    cls_predictions,\n    display_labels=[\"No Default\", \"Default\"]\n)\n\nplt.title(\"Classification: Confusion Matrix\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.569322Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.569652Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.786508Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.56962Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.785312Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":11},{"id":"8e34de19","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual 3 — Classification produces probabilities too\n\nA binary classifier can estimate a probability such as:\n\n> Probability of default = 0.73\n\nA threshold can then convert that probability into a final class.\n\nWe will explore classification thresholds properly in a later day.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"2ae0fa9d","cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n\nplt.hist(\n    cls_probabilities[y_test_cls.to_numpy() == 0],\n    bins=20,\n    alpha=0.6,\n    label=\"Actual: No Default\"\n)\n\nplt.hist(\n    cls_probabilities[y_test_cls.to_numpy() == 1],\n    bins=20,\n    alpha=0.6,\n    label=\"Actual: Default\"\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"Predicted probability of default\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Number of cases\")\nplt.title(\"Classification: Predicted Default Probabilities\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.787651Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.788008Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.024056Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:02.787979Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.023183Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"9332d053","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Part 2 — Regression\n\n## Business question\n\n> **What is the estimated price of this house?**\n\nNow the target is not a class.\n\nThe model receives property-related features such as:\n\n- living area\n- number of bedrooms\n- property age\n- distance from the city center\n- neighborhood quality score\n\nand predicts a numerical value such as:\n\n- ₹42 lakh\n- ₹78 lakh\n- ₹1.15 crore\n\nBecause the target can take many numerical values on a continuous scale, this is a **regression** problem.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"40515a0c","cell_type":"code","source":"# Generate a synthetic housing-style dataset\n\nn_houses = 1800\n\narea_sqft = np.random.normal(1450, 450, n_houses).clip(450, 4000)\nbedrooms = np.random.randint(1, 6, n_houses)\nproperty_age_years = np.random.randint(0, 45, n_houses)\ndistance_city_km = np.random.gamma(2.2, 4.0, n_houses).clip(0.5, 35)\nneighborhood_score = np.random.uniform(1, 10, n_houses)\n\n# Synthetic price formula for teaching only.\nprice_lakh = (\n    8\n    + 0.035 * area_sqft\n    + 3.0 * bedrooms\n    - 0.35 * property_age_years\n    - 0.55 * distance_city_km\n    + 4.5 * neighborhood_score\n    + np.random.normal(0, 8, n_houses)\n)\n\nprice_lakh = price_lakh.clip(12, None)\n\nhousing_df = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"area_sqft\": area_sqft.round(0),\n    \"bedrooms\": bedrooms,\n    \"property_age_years\": property_age_years,\n    \"distance_city_km\": distance_city_km.round(2),\n    \"neighborhood_score\": neighborhood_score.round(2),\n    \"price_lakh\": price_lakh.round(2)\n})\n\nhousing_df.head()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.025194Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.025534Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.048669Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.025508Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.047838Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":13,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"   area_sqft  bedrooms  property_age_years  distance_city_km  \\\n0     1357.0         5                  43              6.16   \n1     2110.0         2                  26              4.90   \n2     1839.0         5                  25              7.05   \n3     1821.0         2                  19             10.42   \n4     1505.0         4                  12              4.16   \n\n   neighborhood_score  price_lakh  \n0                5.70       96.00  \n1                2.89       89.80  \n2                7.01      118.39  \n3                5.94       91.67  \n4                8.23       94.00  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>area_sqft</th>\n      <th>bedrooms</th>\n      <th>property_age_years</th>\n      <th>distance_city_km</th>\n      <th>neighborhood_score</th>\n      <th>price_lakh</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>1357.0</td>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>43</td>\n      <td>6.16</td>\n      <td>5.70</td>\n      <td>96.00</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>2110.0</td>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>26</td>\n      <td>4.90</td>\n      <td>2.89</td>\n      <td>89.80</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>1839.0</td>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>25</td>\n      <td>7.05</td>\n      <td>7.01</td>\n      <td>118.39</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>1821.0</td>\n      <td>2</td>\n      <td>19</td>\n      <td>10.42</td>\n      <td>5.94</td>\n      <td>91.67</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>1505.0</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>12</td>\n      <td>4.16</td>\n      <td>8.23</td>\n      <td>94.00</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":13},{"id":"671f64f9","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual 4 — What are we predicting?\n\nHere we plot **house area** against **house price**.\n\nUnlike classification, there are no two classes to separate.\n\nThe target itself is a number.\n\nThe model is trying to learn how the features relate to the final numerical value.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"567a196e","cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n\nplt.scatter(\n    housing_df[\"area_sqft\"],\n    housing_df[\"price_lakh\"],\n    alpha=0.45\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"Area (sq ft)\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Price (lakh)\")\nplt.title(\"Regression target: Predicting a Continuous House Value\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.050017Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.050429Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.276257Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.050391Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.2751Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":14},{"id":"2001ec1c","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Train a regression model\n\nWe use **Linear Regression** as a simple baseline.\n\nAgain, the goal today is not to go deeply into the mathematics of linear regression.  \nThat will come in a later notebook.\n\nToday we are focusing on the difference between **predicting a class** and **predicting a quantity**.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"39a499de","cell_type":"code","source":"regression_features = [\n    \"area_sqft\",\n    \"bedrooms\",\n    \"property_age_years\",\n    \"distance_city_km\",\n    \"neighborhood_score\"\n]\n\nX_reg = housing_df[regression_features]\ny_reg = housing_df[\"price_lakh\"]\n\nX_train_reg, X_test_reg, y_train_reg, y_test_reg = train_test_split(\n    X_reg,\n    y_reg,\n    test_size=0.20,\n    random_state=42\n)\n\nregression_model = make_pipeline(\n    StandardScaler(),\n    LinearRegression()\n)\n\nregression_model.fit(X_train_reg, y_train_reg)\n\nreg_predictions = regression_model.predict(X_test_reg)\n\nmae = mean_absolute_error(y_test_reg, reg_predictions)\nrmse = mean_squared_error(y_test_reg, reg_predictions) ** 0.5\nr2 = r2_score(y_test_reg, reg_predictions)\n\nprint(\"MAE:\", round(mae, 2), \"lakh\")\nprint(\"RMSE:\", round(rmse, 2), \"lakh\")\nprint(\"R²:\", round(r2, 3))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.278744Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.2792Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.302454Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.279168Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.301441Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"MAE: 6.3 lakh\nRMSE: 8.11 lakh\nR²: 0.865\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":15},{"id":"3edaa198","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual 5 — Actual vs predicted house values\n\nThis is one of the most useful regression visualizations.\n\n- X-axis = actual value\n- Y-axis = predicted value\n- dashed diagonal = perfect prediction\n\nIf a point lies exactly on the diagonal line, the prediction matches the actual value.\n\nThe farther a point is from the line, the larger the prediction error.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"5c1e3a82","cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(7, 7))\n\nplt.scatter(\n    y_test_reg,\n    reg_predictions,\n    alpha=0.5\n)\n\nminimum = min(y_test_reg.min(), reg_predictions.min())\nmaximum = max(y_test_reg.max(), reg_predictions.max())\n\nplt.plot(\n    [minimum, maximum],\n    [minimum, maximum],\n    linestyle=\"--\",\n    label=\"Perfect prediction\"\n)\n\nplt.xlabel(\"Actual house value (lakh)\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Predicted house value (lakh)\")\nplt.title(\"Regression: Actual vs Predicted Values\")\nplt.legend()\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.303986Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.305131Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.547939Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.305096Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.546804Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 700x700 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":16},{"id":"e74c01b6","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visual 6 — Residuals\n\nA residual is:\n\n**Actual value − Predicted value**\n\nResiduals help us understand *how wrong* individual numerical predictions are.\n\nA well-behaved simple regression model should ideally have errors scattered around zero rather than showing a strong systematic pattern.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"fa59712e","cell_type":"code","source":"residuals = y_test_reg.to_numpy() - reg_predictions\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n\nplt.scatter(\n    reg_predictions,\n    residuals,\n    alpha=0.5\n)\n\nplt.axhline(0, linestyle=\"--\")\n\nplt.xlabel(\"Predicted house value (lakh)\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Residual = Actual - Predicted\")\nplt.title(\"Regression: Residual Plot\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.549183Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.549593Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.757197Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.549563Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-08-08T18:05:03.756109Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":17},{"id":"832eb7e8","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Classification vs Regression — Final comparison\n\n| Question | Classification | Regression |\n|---|---|---|\n| What does it predict? | A class/category | A continuous numerical value |\n| Example | Default / No Default | Estimated house value |\n| Example model | Logistic Regression | Linear Regression |\n| Useful visual | Confusion matrix / probability distribution | Actual vs predicted / residual plot |\n| Example metric | Precision, Recall, F1, Accuracy | MAE, RMSE, R² |\n\n## Key takeaway\n\n> **Classification answers: “Which class?”**  \n> **Regression answers: “How much?”**\n\nThe distinction starts with the target we are trying to predict.\n\nThe algorithm, evaluation metric, and visualization then follow from that problem definition.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"6c6e7252","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Limitations\n\n1. Both datasets are synthetic and were created only to make the concepts visually understandable.\n2. The default-risk formula is not a real credit-scoring or underwriting policy.\n3. The housing-price formula is not a real valuation methodology.\n4. Accuracy alone is not sufficient for evaluating real risk-classification systems.\n5. Linear Regression and Logistic Regression are used as simple baselines; production systems may require very different models, controls, validation, and governance.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"8a82a0f2","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# References\n\n## Supervised learning\nGoogle Machine Learning — Supervised Learning  \nhttps://developers.google.com/machine-learning/intro-to-ml/supervised\n\nScikit-learn — Supervised learning  \nhttps://scikit-learn.org/stable/supervised_learning.html\n\n## Classification\nScikit-learn — Logistic Regression  \nhttps://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression.html\n\nScikit-learn — Classification metrics  \nhttps://scikit-learn.org/stable/api/sklearn.metrics.html\n\n## Regression\nScikit-learn — Linear Regression  \nhttps://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.linear_model.LinearRegression.html\n\nScikit-learn — Regression metrics  \nhttps://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/model_evaluation.html#regression-metrics\n","metadata":{}}]}